{% extends 'shared/layouts/base.njk' %}
{% block main %}
    {% include 'partials/bigger-banner.njk' %}

    <div class="jh-wrap" id="content">
        <h1 class="jh-page-title">Meet the Musicians</h1>

        <section class="px-box" id="ensemble-intro" aria-labelledby="message">
            <h2 class="px-title" id="message">A message from Justin</h2>
            <div class="jh-prose">
            <p>
            What constitutes... mutability? In a band?
            </p>
            <p>
            Every time I take the stage and every time I put on cans in the
            studio, I seek to make a new instance of the class Band. Our setlist is unique each night; our
            arrangements and effects are often chosen (and signaled to one another) in the moment.
            </p>
            <p>
            In my journey to write logic that is the internet I want to see - from hacking together a viable
            battlestation for myself to play games with my kiddo, to legacy enterprise web apps, to custom dapps for
            this band and production, I have had many notions in my head (sometimes literally in my dreams) about mutability and
            its role in mapping the metaphor of the mind into a codebase, and particularly object orientation.
            </p>
            <p>
            Some of the most important friends I've made during these years of deliberation are those who have chosen to play (and sometimes
            write) music with me.
            </p>
            <p>
            And their contributions don't seem to me to be a small part of some persistent monolith that belongs to me;
            instead, they feel each like their own distinct and complete creation.
            </p>
            <p>
            So what follows is a list of those people, with links to their contributions, and in some cases, a brief anecdote about our meeting.  This list is sorted by the number of instances they have appeared in, with extra weight given to studio recordings.
            </p>
            </div>
        </section>

        {# First, as it has always been, Justin is left off: it's his list. Those he has written about
           come first, each in a box; everyone else follows, together. #}
        {% set flip = [] %}
        {% for name, metadata in pickers_by_instance_count.slice(1) %}
            {% set details = ensemble[name] %}
            {% if details %}
            {% set turn = flip.push(name) %}
            {% set who = metadata %}{# set, so the partials below can see it: a loop's unpacked names don't reach an include #}
            <section class="px-box person-info" aria-labelledby="picker-{{ loop.index }}">
                <h2 class="px-title" id="picker-{{ loop.index }}">{{ name }}</h2>
                <div class="jh-picker{% if not details.Photo %} jh-picker--plain{% elif flip.length % 2 == 0 %} jh-picker--flip{% endif %}">
                    {% if details.Photo %}
                    <figure class="jh-picker-photo">
                        <a class="spotlight" href="{{ get_image(details.Photo) }}" title="{{ details.Caption }}">
                            <img src="{{ get_image(details.Photo) }}" alt="{{ details.Caption }}" loading="lazy"/>
                        </a>
                        <figcaption>{{ details.Caption }}</figcaption>
                    </figure>
                    {% endif %}
                    <div>
                        {% include 'partials/picker-stats.njk' %}
                        <p class="person-bio">{{ details.Description }}</p>
                        {% include 'partials/picker-links.njk' %}
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>
            {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}

        <section class="px-box" aria-labelledby="everyone">
            <h2 class="px-title" id="everyone">And everyone else who has been on one</h2>
            <ul class="jh-party">
                {% for name, metadata in pickers_by_instance_count.slice(1) %}
                {% if not ensemble[name] %}
                <li>
                    <a class="jh-party-name" href="{{ basePath }}{{ metadata.resource_url }}">{{ name }}</a>
                    <span class="jh-party-plays">{{ metadata.instruments_display }}</span>
                    <span class="jh-party-count">{{ metadata.total_instance_count }} instance{% if metadata.total_instance_count != 1 %}s{% endif %}</span>
                    {% if metadata.pickipedia_url or metadata.bacon_url %}
                    <span class="jh-party-plays">{% if metadata.pickipedia_url %}<a href="{{ metadata.pickipedia_url }}">PickiPedia</a>{% endif %}{% if metadata.pickipedia_url and metadata.bacon_url %} · {% endif %}{% if metadata.bacon_url %}<a href="{{ metadata.bacon_url }}">the Oracle</a>{% endif %}</span>
                    {% endif %}
                </li>
                {% endif %}
                {% endfor %}
            </ul>
        </section>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
